## Likely follow-up questions

**Q: Why a ticket per entry?**

A uniform pick over tickets is a weighted pick over members — no prefix sums needed.

**Q: RemoveTicket the last ticket in the list?**

The "moved" ticket is the removed one: update the set before deleting, or handle pos == last.

**Q: Complexity?**

O(1) average for all three; O(total tickets) memory.

**Q: Memory per member instead of per ticket?**

Then picks need prefix sums: a Fenwick tree gives O(log n) for everything.

**Q: Many threads.**

Each operation touches two structures, so one lock around each; Random is not thread-safe either.

**Q: A billion tickets across services.**

Shard by member; pick a shard by its total tickets, then pick inside it — two-level weighting.

**Q: Related?**

InterviewDB Q12 (random data structure) and LeetCode 381 — the same swap-with-last trick.

